Accept non-constant initializers of GLSL ES globals under allow_glsl_relaxed_es, and turn the
option on by default.

GLSL ES 1.00 section 4.3 requires the initializer of a global without a storage qualifier to be
a constant expression, and Mesa rejects anything else. The PowerVR SGX compiler on the WT1H
accepted it, and firmware QML relies on that: StarfishComponents/Parallelogram.qml (the launcher's
slanted panels) and Eos/Items/Parallelogram.qml declare, at global scope,

    highp float blurR = 1.0 - blur;          // blur is a uniform
    highp float x = qt_TexCoord0.x;          // a varying

On Mesa the ShaderEffect fails to compile, and Qt 5.0's QQuickCustomMaterialShader falls back to
"gl_FragColor = vec4(1., 0., 1., 1.)": the panels come out solid #FF00FF.

With the option on, such a global is handled as in desktop GLSL 1.20: the initializer runs at the
top of main(). The option's existing effects (precision mismatches of uniforms across stages,
mixed ES versions in one program, dFdx/dFdy without OES_standard_derivatives) are leniencies the
SGX driver had as well. Set allow_glsl_relaxed_es=false in the environment to get stock Mesa.

--- a/src/compiler/glsl/ast_to_hir.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/glsl/ast_to_hir.cpp
@@ -4790,10 +4790,15 @@
     *     executed.  Such initializers must be a constant expression."
     *
     * The same section of the GLSL ES 3.00.4 spec has similar language.
+    *
+    * allow_glsl_relaxed_es lifts that rule for globals without a storage
+    * qualifier, as desktop GLSL 1.20 does: the initializer runs at the top of
+    * main(). Some GLSL ES compilers (PowerVR SGX) accept such shaders.
     */
    if (type->qualifier.flags.q.constant
        || type->qualifier.flags.q.uniform
-       || (state->es_shader && state->current_function == NULL)) {
+       || (state->es_shader && state->current_function == NULL &&
+           !state->consts->AllowGLSLRelaxedES)) {
       ir_rvalue *new_rhs = validate_assignment(state, initializer_loc,
                                                lhs, rhs, true);
       if (new_rhs != NULL) {
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/pipe-loader/driinfo_gallium.h
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/pipe-loader/driinfo_gallium.h
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
    DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_120_SUBSET_IN_110(false)
    DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_EMBEDDED_STRUCTURE_DECLARATIONS(false)
    DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_BUILTIN_CONST_EXPRESSION(false)
-   DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_RELAXED_ES(false)
+   DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_RELAXED_ES(true)
    DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_BUILTIN_VARIABLE_REDECLARATION(false)
    DRI_CONF_ALLOW_GLSL_CROSS_STAGE_INTERPOLATION_MISMATCH(false)
    DRI_CONF_DO_DCE_BEFORE_CLIP_CULL_ANALYSIS(false)
